# Cloudflare Pages _headers
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# Syntax is whitespace-sensitive: a path on its own line, then each header indented
# beneath it. A malformed file is ignored in full rather than partially, so verify the
# served response rather than assuming.

# RFC 8288 Link header for agent discovery. `describedby` means "a resource providing
# information about the link's context", which is exactly what /organization.jsonld is.
#
# Only this one relation is published. Scanners also ask for api-catalog, service-desc
# and service-doc — all three describe APIs, and this site has no public API. An empty
# /.well-known/api-catalog would give an agent that followed it nothing at all, which is
# worse than not advertising one.
#
# Cloudflare Early Hints emits its OWN Link header carrying the font preconnects,
# synthesised from the <link rel="preconnect"> tags in Base.astro, and replays it as a
# 103 before the HTML arrives. Setting Link here does NOT replace it — both headers are
# sent, which RFC 8288 allows.
#
# Worth stating because the first measurement said otherwise: on a fresh deploy only
# this header appeared, and the preconnects looked dropped. That was a cold Early Hints
# cache, not a replacement. Duplicating the preconnects here to "restore" them was
# unnecessary and added a copy that would drift from Base.astro.
/
  Link: </organization.jsonld>; rel="describedby"; type="application/ld+json"

# Cloudflare types static files from their extension and does not know `.jsonld`, so
# without this the description is served as a download rather than as JSON-LD.
/organization.jsonld
  Content-Type: application/ld+json; charset=utf-8
